  {
    "paragraph_index": 6,
    "paragraph": "“It's really isolating to have a lot of money. People's reactions to you can be scary,” said Barbara Nusbaum, an expert in money psychology. “We are all taught not to talk about money. It's not polite to talk about money. Ironically, it's harder to talk about having money than it is to talk about not having money. It's much more socially acceptable to say ‘I am broke. Things are hard.' You can't say ‘I have a ton of money.' You have to keep a lot of your life private.” As a result, Cockrell points out, the rich tend to hang out with other rich Americans, not out of snobbery but in order to be around those who understand them and their problems.",
